WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:09.541
[wind whistling]

2
00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:11.916
[baby crying]

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.916
[clattering]

4
00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:25.250
[thunder rumbling]

5
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:27.875
[tense dramatic music playing]

6
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:47.791
[bell ringing]

7
00:01:02.291 --> 00:01:04.416
[music intensifies]

8
00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:15.958
[narrator] <i>At that prodigious instant.</i>

9
00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:21.791
<i>Melquiades' final keys were revealed</i>
<i>to Aureliano Babilonia.</i>

10
00:01:22.541 --> 00:01:25.625
<i>He saw the epigraph of the parchments</i>
<i>perfectly placed</i>

11
00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:28.208
<i>in the order of man's time and space.</i>

12
00:01:28.916 --> 00:01:31.750
<i>The first of the line is tied to a tree.</i>

13
00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:36.375
<i>and the last is being eaten by ants.</i>

14
00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:41.958
ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE

15
00:01:42.041 --> 00:01:44.041
[footsteps approaching]

16
00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:48.125
[tense music playing]

17
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.500
[narrator] <i>At the center</i>
<i>of the chalk circle only he could enter.</i>

18
00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:13.833
<i>Colonel Aureliano Buendía decided</i>
<i>with brief and unappealable orders</i>

19
00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:15.291
<i>the fate of the world.</i>

20
00:02:15.375 --> 00:02:16.625
[distant shouting]

21
00:02:16.708 --> 00:02:18.208
- [man] Colonel?
- Hmm?

22
00:02:18.708 --> 00:02:20.875
There are some women outside
that wanna talk to you.

23
00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:22.250
Well. let 'em wait.

24
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:24.125
[woman 1] This is a peaceful protest!

25
00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:27.333
- Aureliano José?
- Yes. sir?

26
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:29.125
Where are my tweezers?

27
00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:33.625
[women chanting] Release General Moncada!
Release General Moncada!

28
00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:37.000
Release General Moncada!
Release General Moncada!

29
00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:39.083
[chanting continues]

30
00:02:42.041 --> 00:02:44.000
Release General Moncada!

31
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:45.791
Release General Moncada!

32
00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:47.791
Release General Moncada!

33
00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:49.875
[chanting continues]

34
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.666
[chanting subsides]

35
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.916
[woman 2] Moncada is innocent!
Set him free!

36
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.250
[woman 1] Release him!

37
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.916
Ladies.

38
00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.041
you are all violating curfew.

39
00:03:05.708 --> 00:03:06.666
Go home already.

40
00:03:07.333 --> 00:03:09.708
You've taken back Macondo. Aureliano.

41
00:03:10.916 --> 00:03:12.583
Why is that not enough for you?

42
00:03:14.625 --> 00:03:17.000
If you've got something else
that you'd like to say.

43
00:03:17.666 --> 00:03:20.500
then file a formal petition
with the Council of War.

44
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:22.250
Good afternoon.

45
00:03:22.333 --> 00:03:24.833
You can talk down to us all you want.

46
00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:28.375
But don't you forget. Aureliano.

47
00:03:29.958 --> 00:03:33.041
that as long as God keeps me
on this earth. I'm your mother.

48
00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:35.791
And no matter how revolutionary you are.

49
00:03:35.875 --> 00:03:38.583
I can still pull down your pants
and give you a proper whipping

50
00:03:38.666 --> 00:03:39.916
if I have to!

51
00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:42.791
Release General Moncada!

52
00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:46.458
[chanting] Release General Moncada!
Release General Moncada!

53
00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:48.041
- Release General Moncada!
- Right.

54
00:03:48.125 --> 00:03:50.208
Release General Moncada!

55
00:03:51.166 --> 00:03:53.000
Release General Moncada!

56
00:03:53.083 --> 00:03:54.958
[chanting continues]

57
00:03:55.041 --> 00:03:56.250
[woman 1] Stop pushing me!

58
00:03:56.333 --> 00:03:58.250
[man 1] Hey. stop pushing. ladies!

59
00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:00.750
- [woman 1] Release him!
- [man 1] Stop it!

60
00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:02.333
[man 2] Is your fear of death so great

61
00:04:02.416 --> 00:04:04.833
that you can't even speak to a man
who's been condemned to it?

62
00:04:04.916 --> 00:04:06.708
[Úrsula] Release him right now!

63
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.666
[man 1] Ma'am. stop resisting.
or we're gonna arrest you too!

64
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.291
[woman 3] You monster!

65
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.208
[man 3] That's enough! That's enough!
Everybody go home!

66
00:04:15.916 --> 00:04:17.125
That's right.

67
00:04:18.875 --> 00:04:21.208
Look me in the eyes
before you take my life.

68
00:04:21.708 --> 00:04:23.666
Make no mistake. José Raquel.

69
00:04:24.291 --> 00:04:25.916
I did not sentence you.

70
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.916
The revolution sentenced you.

71
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.541
Go to hell. Aureliano.

72
00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:36.791
You know as well as I do
that these war councils are a farce.

73
00:04:38.125 --> 00:04:40.708
Hmm. Let me ask you this.

74
00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.791
Wouldn't you have done
the same thing in my place?

75
00:04:47.041 --> 00:04:48.041
Probably.

76
00:04:48.958 --> 00:04:49.791
Yeah.

77
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:52.625
But this isn't about my execution.

78
00:04:52.708 --> 00:04:54.916
The thing that really concerns me

79
00:04:55.416 --> 00:04:58.250
is that. for how much you say
you despise the military.

80
00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:01.500
you've become just like them.

81
00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:04.958
- [Aureliano] Hmm.
- Mm.

82
00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:08.208
[uneasy music playing]

83
00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:20.666
[whistle blows]

84
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.791
[man] Citizens of Macondo!

85
00:05:24.375 --> 00:05:26.208
[two whistle blasts]

86
00:05:26.708 --> 00:05:29.333
[man] A curfew is in place across town.

87
00:05:31.041 --> 00:05:33.833
No one is allowed to go outside.

88
00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:36.208
Where are you going at this hour?

89
00:05:36.291 --> 00:05:37.708
[man] There will be no exceptions!

90
00:05:37.791 --> 00:05:39.166
To see the execution.

91
00:05:39.666 --> 00:05:41.291
Didn't you hear? There's curfew.

92
00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:43.666
Do you want to come?

93
00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.333
- Why would you wanna see that?
- [whistle blows]

94
00:05:48.833 --> 00:05:50.875
That's how our father died.

95
00:05:50.958 --> 00:05:54.083
[narrator] <i>José Arcadio Segundo</i>
<i>and Aureliano Segundo</i>

96
00:05:54.166 --> 00:05:56.500
<i>looked like a trick of mirrors.</i>

97
00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.916
<i>They were so much alike</i>

98
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.250
<i>that not even Santa Sofía de la Piedad.</i>
<i>their mother. could tell them apart.</i>

99
00:06:04.333 --> 00:06:06.333
[uneasy music continues]

100
00:06:09.125 --> 00:06:10.541
[man 2] Soldiers!

101
00:06:17.375 --> 00:06:18.541
Ready!

102
00:06:20.416 --> 00:06:21.500
[rifles cock]

103
00:06:21.583 --> 00:06:25.375
[woman] Our Father. who art in heaven.
hallowed be thy name.

104
00:06:25.458 --> 00:06:30.083
Thy kingdom come. thy will be done
on earth as it is in heaven.

105
00:06:30.708 --> 00:06:31.958
[man 2] Aim!

106
00:06:33.041 --> 00:06:35.791
[music intensifies]

107
00:06:39.708 --> 00:06:41.583
- [man 2] Fire!
- [gunshots]

108
00:06:52.666 --> 00:06:53.750
- [distant gunshot]
- [gasps]

109
00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:55.000
[gunshot]

110
00:07:02.708 --> 00:07:05.625
- [José Arcadio II] He's alive! He's alive.
- [man 2] Soldiers. take him away!

111
00:07:05.708 --> 00:07:07.333
- [man 3] Hey. stop him!
- He's still alive!

112
00:07:07.416 --> 00:07:09.125
[man 3] It's the colonel's nephew.

113
00:07:09.666 --> 00:07:11.291
[José Arcadio II] He's still alive!

114
00:07:11.375 --> 00:07:13.416
- [man 2] Grab him!
- You're gonna bury him alive!

115
00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.583
- Come on.
- Murderer!

116
00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:15.791
[man 2] Restrain him!

117
00:07:15.875 --> 00:07:16.875
Stop moving!

118
00:07:16.958 --> 00:07:18.208
- [man 2] Take him away!
- Stop!

119
00:07:18.291 --> 00:07:21.166
- He's alive! He's alive!
- Let's go. Come on.

120
00:07:21.833 --> 00:07:23.541
[José Arcadio II] Murderers!

121
00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:25.416
You're gonna bury him alive!

122
00:07:26.583 --> 00:07:28.041
He's still alive!

123
00:07:28.125 --> 00:07:30.375
[melancholy music playing]

124
00:07:30.458 --> 00:07:32.416
[José Arcadio II] You're all murderers!

125
00:07:34.083 --> 00:07:36.541
[breathing heavily]
[melancholy music continues]

126
00:07:37.416 --> 00:07:39.416
[bell ringing]

127
00:07:42.375 --> 00:07:44.291
[narrator] <i>The death of General Moncada</i>

128
00:07:44.375 --> 00:07:47.250
<i>made such an impression</i>
<i>on José Arcadio Segundo</i>

129
00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:50.666
<i>that from then on. he detested war.</i>

130
00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:53.833
<i>and he decided to take refuge</i>
<i>in the town church.</i>

131
00:07:53.916 --> 00:07:55.666
[women whisper prayers]

132
00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.541
[father] <i>We are gathered here today</i>

133
00:07:57.625 --> 00:08:00.291
<i>to pay tribute to a great man.</i>

134
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:05.416
<i>whom God has called back</i>
<i>to his kingdom this morning.</i>

135
00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:09.250
General José Raquel Moncada.

136
00:08:09.333 --> 00:08:11.000
[man 1] God didn't call him. Father.

137
00:08:11.083 --> 00:08:13.625
He was murdered
by those god-forsaken Liberals.

138
00:08:13.708 --> 00:08:15.583
- [man 2] That's right.
- The colonel killed him!

139
00:08:15.666 --> 00:08:17.625
[man 3] The colonel's a murderer!

140
00:08:17.708 --> 00:08:19.125
[man 4] He's a murderer!

141
00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:20.750
Silence. all of you!

142
00:08:22.375 --> 00:08:24.583
We are still in the house of God.

143
00:08:26.333 --> 00:08:28.250
not in some public square.

144
00:08:30.833 --> 00:08:32.833
[tense music playing]

145
00:08:35.208 --> 00:08:39.791
[narrator] <i>Meanwhile.</i>
<i>while lost in a book he'd found.</i>

146
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.166
<i>Aureliano Segundo</i>
<i>instantly recognized Melquiades.</i>

147
00:08:46.541 --> 00:08:47.750
Hello. young man.

148
00:08:47.833 --> 00:08:49.750
[narrator] <i>The old gypsy was a memory</i>

149
00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:53.333
<i>that had been passed down</i>
<i>from generation to generation</i>

150
00:08:53.416 --> 00:08:56.041
<i>and had reached him</i>
<i>through his grandfather.</i>

151
00:08:58.458 --> 00:08:59.375
What is this?

152
00:08:59.458 --> 00:09:02.000
[narrator] <i>From then on.</i>
<i>they met every afternoon.</i>

153
00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.875
<i>Melquiades spoke to him of the world.</i>

154
00:09:05.375 --> 00:09:08.500
<i>He tried to impress upon him</i>
<i>his old wisdom</i>

155
00:09:08.583 --> 00:09:11.500
<i>but refused to translate the manuscripts.</i>

156
00:09:11.583 --> 00:09:13.958
<i>for their meaning was not to be understood</i>

157
00:09:14.041 --> 00:09:16.666
<i>until a hundred years had passed.</i>

158
00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:17.958
[music fades]

159
00:09:20.041 --> 00:09:22.583
[woman] Sir. could you help me?
[man] Of course. What do you need?

160
00:09:22.666 --> 00:09:24.666
[woman] May I please have five of these?

161
00:09:26.291 --> 00:09:28.291
[music turns ominous]

162
00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:37.250
[woman 1] You wouldn't believe
how much they've grown.

163
00:09:37.333 --> 00:09:38.958
[woman 2] See you both tomorrow. then?

164
00:09:39.041 --> 00:09:41.625
[woman 1] We'll be there nice and early
so we can discuss.

165
00:09:41.708 --> 00:09:43.416
- [woman 2] Mm-hmm.
- See you.

166
00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.500
[tense percussive music playing]

167
00:10:29.125 --> 00:10:31.625
"And it is my honor
to continue to strengthen the ties

168
00:10:31.708 --> 00:10:34.916
that make us proud
to belong to this corner of the world."

169
00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.208
Who writes this bullshit?

170
00:10:46.625 --> 00:10:47.541
[clears throat]

171
00:10:48.208 --> 00:10:49.166
You put sugar in this?

172
00:11:01.166 --> 00:11:02.166
[clears throat]

173
00:11:03.916 --> 00:11:04.916
[clears throat]

174
00:11:06.625 --> 00:11:07.750
[clears throat]

175
00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:09.416
[Aureliano José] Father. what's wrong?

176
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.500
[clears throat]

177
00:11:12.291 --> 00:11:13.791
[grunting]

178
00:11:13.875 --> 00:11:15.916
[Aureliano José] Hey. what is it?

179
00:11:16.541 --> 00:11:18.333
- Help!
- [man] What is it? What happened?

180
00:11:18.875 --> 00:11:20.750
- Breathe. breathe!
- [Gerineldo] Medic!

181
00:11:20.833 --> 00:11:22.791
- Breathe!
- [man] Colonel. what's wrong?

182
00:11:22.875 --> 00:11:24.625
- [man 2] We need a medic!
- Colonel!

183
00:11:24.708 --> 00:11:26.291
[somber music playing]

184
00:11:26.375 --> 00:11:29.083
Mama Úrsula. Aureliano's been poisoned!

185
00:11:30.833 --> 00:11:32.833
[music turns percussive]

186
00:11:36.666 --> 00:11:40.833
Santa Sofía. fetch me a basket of eggs
and vinegar and two sprigs of dill.

187
00:11:42.666 --> 00:11:44.666
[dark ethereal music playing]

188
00:11:55.583 --> 00:11:57.291
[Úrsula] Leave me alone with my son.

189
00:11:59.125 --> 00:12:00.458
Why are you still standing there?

190
00:12:00.541 --> 00:12:02.000
- [man] Come on.
- [Gerineldo] Let's go.

191
00:12:05.916 --> 00:12:07.083
[painful groan]

192
00:12:07.583 --> 00:12:10.333
[groaning]

193
00:12:13.791 --> 00:12:15.333
[gulping]

194
00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.166
[groaning]

195
00:12:28.041 --> 00:12:29.083
[groans]

196
00:12:30.541 --> 00:12:31.666
[groans]

197
00:12:32.958 --> 00:12:34.958
[Aureliano continues groaning]

198
00:12:37.625 --> 00:12:39.625
[Aureliano coughs. vomits]

199
00:12:42.625 --> 00:12:44.625
[Aureliano coughs. vomits]

200
00:12:46.875 --> 00:12:48.875
[panting. groaning]

201
00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.000
[ominous music playing]

202
00:13:05.083 --> 00:13:07.083
[music fades]

203
00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:22.000
[door lock clicks]

204
00:13:24.791 --> 00:13:27.666
[narrator] <i>Remedios the Beauty</i>
<i>had wandered naked through the house</i>

205
00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:29.375
<i>for 20 years…</i>

206
00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:31.708
Go put some clothes on.

207
00:13:32.541 --> 00:13:36.541
<i>…because her nature</i>
<i>would not accept any form of convention.</i>

208
00:13:38.125 --> 00:13:41.500
Aureliano José. forgive her.

209
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.791
She won't stop. It's a bad habit.

210
00:13:44.291 --> 00:13:46.916
It's not a habit. Mama. It's too hot.

211
00:13:48.708 --> 00:13:50.125
[Sofía] How's your father?

212
00:13:51.791 --> 00:13:53.250
Grandma's still with him.

213
00:13:53.958 --> 00:13:56.333
They gave him enough strychnine
to put a horse down.

214
00:13:56.416 --> 00:13:59.250
but Úrsula says he'll survive.

215
00:14:00.083 --> 00:14:03.666
Amen. I can get your room ready
if you'd like to spend the night.

216
00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:05.250
No. No. thank you.

217
00:14:08.333 --> 00:14:09.666
Just picking something up.

218
00:14:10.166 --> 00:14:11.458
Are my things still here?

219
00:14:13.208 --> 00:14:15.291
Mama Úrsula won't let us touch anything.

220
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.625
She's still holding out hope
that you'll come to your senses soon.

221
00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:26.416
Excuse me.

222
00:14:26.916 --> 00:14:28.000
Go ahead.

223
00:14:31.083 --> 00:14:34.375
[narrator] <i>Aureliano José knew then</i>
<i>what he had to do</i>

224
00:14:35.125 --> 00:14:38.500
<i>because he was no longer some child</i>
<i>afraid of the dark.</i>

225
00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.166
<i>but an animal of the barracks.</i>

226
00:14:41.791 --> 00:14:42.875
[Amaranta] Who is it?

227
00:14:43.625 --> 00:14:44.666
Amaranta. it's me.

228
00:14:48.333 --> 00:14:49.416
Let me in.

229
00:15:05.916 --> 00:15:07.916
[both moaning]

230
00:15:15.041 --> 00:15:15.916
No. wait.

231
00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.958
Sh. Listen to me. all right?

232
00:15:21.625 --> 00:15:24.125
I met a Liberal colonel in battle.

233
00:15:24.625 --> 00:15:26.583
and I told him about me and you.

234
00:15:26.666 --> 00:15:28.750
I always knew you were reckless!

235
00:15:28.833 --> 00:15:30.708
I told him I wanted to marry my aunt.

236
00:15:30.791 --> 00:15:33.041
You're not just reckless. you're a fool!

237
00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.833
He said that's the whole reason
we're at war with the Church.

238
00:15:38.541 --> 00:15:39.833
[Amaranta grunts]

239
00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.166
I did everything
aside from breastfeeding you.

240
00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.083
Raised you like you were my son.

241
00:15:45.583 --> 00:15:46.708
So get out.

242
00:15:47.416 --> 00:15:49.958
I really mean it this time.
Aureliano José.

243
00:15:50.708 --> 00:15:52.000
And don't come back.

244
00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:53.791
Or I'll kill myself.

245
00:15:53.875 --> 00:15:55.875
[tense percussive music playing]

246
00:16:13.208 --> 00:16:15.208
