to consider an armistice."

493
00:33:47.083 --> 00:33:49.666
"In laying down your arms.
the government ensures you a future

494
00:33:49.750 --> 00:33:52.208
where your legacy will be known
not for conflict.

495
00:33:52.291 --> 00:33:54.458
but rather for the heroism
of lasting peace."

496
00:33:57.125 --> 00:33:58.291
[coughs]

497
00:34:03.541 --> 00:34:04.500
[man chuckles]

498
00:34:08.833 --> 00:34:11.750
Dear Mr. President.

499
00:34:12.583 --> 00:34:13.541
Comma.

500
00:34:16.125 --> 00:34:18.041
If I may say so respectfully…

501
00:34:21.333 --> 00:34:23.875
you can go straight to hell

502
00:34:23.958 --> 00:34:26.041
and take your armistice with you.

503
00:34:26.125 --> 00:34:27.500
[tense music stinger]

504
00:34:44.791 --> 00:34:45.916
[sighs]

505
00:34:46.958 --> 00:34:48.958
[tense music playing]

506
00:34:50.291 --> 00:34:53.750
[narrator] <i>Adrift in the loneliness</i>
<i>of his immeasurable power.</i>

507
00:34:53.833 --> 00:34:55.208
<i>he began to lose his way.</i>

508
00:34:58.000 --> 00:35:01.208
<i>His orders were carried out</i>
<i>before they were ever given.</i>

509
00:35:01.708 --> 00:35:03.875
<i>before he had conceived them.</i>

510
00:35:05.458 --> 00:35:09.375
<i>And they always went much further</i>
<i>than what he intended.</i>

511
00:35:13.416 --> 00:35:16.458
[street vendor] Get your paper!
All your regional and capital news here!

512
00:35:16.541 --> 00:35:18.083
[woman] I'll take one. Felipe.

513
00:35:19.250 --> 00:35:21.041
[Felipe] Get your paper!

514
00:35:24.083 --> 00:35:26.083
[uneasy music playing]

515
00:35:30.291 --> 00:35:33.666
[woman] I've got vegetables.
fruit. onions…

516
00:35:33.750 --> 00:35:35.375
"Aureliano Buendía…

517
00:35:35.458 --> 00:35:38.250
[street vendors shouting indistinctly]

518
00:35:38.333 --> 00:35:41.375
…the subversive group leader
in the Caribbean.

519
00:35:42.208 --> 00:35:46.125
unleashes violence and sends
macabre message to the president."

520
00:35:46.208 --> 00:35:48.208
[somber music playing]

521
00:35:50.291 --> 00:35:52.166
[man] <i>"There's reason to believe</i>

522
00:35:53.208 --> 00:35:57.833
<i>that it was Colonel Buendía himself</i>
<i>who decapitated the emissary.</i>

523
00:35:59.625 --> 00:36:03.708
thus sending his grim message
to the president of the republic."

524
00:36:04.583 --> 00:36:05.833
[music fades]

525
00:36:05.916 --> 00:36:09.666
[Pilar] "His message.
an utter rejection of an armistice.

526
00:36:10.500 --> 00:36:13.541
has shocked the entire country."

527
00:36:14.625 --> 00:36:16.166
- Aureliano.
- Hmm?

528
00:36:16.250 --> 00:36:17.875
You shouldn't go out tonight.

529
00:36:18.375 --> 00:36:21.291
There's gonna be trouble
after this thing with your father.

530
00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:24.000
Don't worry.
I'm just going to the theater.

531
00:36:27.208 --> 00:36:29.083
There's someone I want you to meet.

532
00:36:29.166 --> 00:36:31.000
Oh yeah? Who?

533
00:36:32.000 --> 00:36:33.166
Stay here.

534
00:36:33.708 --> 00:36:35.708
I'll set up a time for you to meet her.

535
00:36:38.541 --> 00:36:41.000
I promise I'll be home early.
I'll meet her then.

536
00:36:44.916 --> 00:36:46.916
[dramatic string music playing]

537
00:36:49.333 --> 00:36:50.208
[sighs]

538
00:36:50.958 --> 00:36:53.333
Tomorrow. we leave for Asturias.

539
00:36:53.416 --> 00:36:56.708
Portugal. who once gave us asylum.
will grant us safe passage.

540
00:36:56.791 --> 00:36:58.166
Till tomorrow. then.

541
00:36:58.250 --> 00:37:00.458
Sleep well. Sleep. my friend.

542
00:37:00.541 --> 00:37:03.666
Sir. will you keep vigil over my sleep?

543
00:37:04.208 --> 00:37:06.833
From now on.
you and I are one and the same.

544
00:37:06.916 --> 00:37:09.666
- But. sir…
- Leave me be until dawn.

545
00:37:11.083 --> 00:37:13.500
There I have lost all that I have loved.

546
00:37:13.583 --> 00:37:14.875
- [actor 1] So have I.
- So have I.

547
00:37:14.958 --> 00:37:16.833
[actor 2] Fathers. brothers…

548
00:37:17.750 --> 00:37:19.250
- So have I.
- [man] Sh.

549
00:37:19.333 --> 00:37:21.791
- [actor 1] I've been betrayed too.
- [actor 2] I had to flee.

550
00:37:21.875 --> 00:37:23.125
[actor 1] I expect nothing.

551
00:37:23.208 --> 00:37:24.375
Neither do I.

552
00:37:24.458 --> 00:37:27.041
[actor 2] At times. I think about
horrible acts of revenge.

553
00:37:28.750 --> 00:37:31.000
- Is that dagger yours?
- Yes.

554
00:37:31.083 --> 00:37:33.583
[actor 3] That dagger shall be
the death of Conservatives.

555
00:37:33.666 --> 00:37:35.125
- [actor 2] I'm Conservative!
- So am I!

556
00:37:35.208 --> 00:37:36.583
- [whistles]
- [man] Sh!

557
00:37:36.666 --> 00:37:38.708
- [woman] Stop whistling. Be quiet!
- [man 2] Be quiet.

558
00:37:39.833 --> 00:37:42.125
[actors grunting]

559
00:37:43.875 --> 00:37:45.875
[applause]

560
00:37:45.958 --> 00:37:47.958
[cheering]

561
00:37:52.875 --> 00:37:54.958
You know I've never been to the theater.

562
00:37:55.041 --> 00:37:57.208
Me neither. We'll come back soon.

563
00:37:57.291 --> 00:37:59.083
Go to hell.
you Conservative son of a bitch!

564
00:37:59.166 --> 00:38:01.875
- [woman 1] Hey. watch out!
- [woman 2] Did you see that?

565
00:38:01.958 --> 00:38:03.875
The only son of a bitch here is you!

566
00:38:03.958 --> 00:38:06.000
[man 1] Hey. don't let him push you
around like that.

567
00:38:06.083 --> 00:38:07.416
[man 2] Yeah. fight!

568
00:38:08.791 --> 00:38:11.125
Let the first stone be cast…

569
00:38:13.208 --> 00:38:16.666
by the man who hasn't fucked
his own whore of a mother.

570
00:38:16.750 --> 00:38:18.666
[woman 3] Don't talk about
his mother that way!

571
00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:20.666
Mess with my mother.
and I'll put a bullet in you!

572
00:38:20.750 --> 00:38:22.500
- Conservative bastard!
- Show him who's in charge.

573
00:38:22.583 --> 00:38:26.041
He's more than a son of a bitch.
He's a Buendía.

574
00:38:26.125 --> 00:38:28.875
- [man 3] Out with the Buendías!
- Put that Liberal scum in his place.

575
00:38:28.958 --> 00:38:31.958
Firstborn of the filthiest bastard
this town's ever seen.

576
00:38:32.041 --> 00:38:34.041
[crowd shouting indistinctly]

577
00:38:39.625 --> 00:38:41.625
[both grunting]

578
00:38:42.416 --> 00:38:44.416
[crowd shouting. whistling]

579
00:38:45.916 --> 00:38:47.083
[crowd gasps]

580
00:38:50.250 --> 00:38:52.041
[narrator] <i>Carmelita Montiel.</i>

581
00:38:52.791 --> 00:38:54.500
<i>a twenty-year-old virgin.</i>

582
00:38:54.583 --> 00:38:57.541
<i>had just bathed in orange blossom water.</i>

583
00:38:58.375 --> 00:39:01.791
<i>She was scattering rosemary leaves</i>
<i>on Pilar Ternera's bed</i>

584
00:39:01.875 --> 00:39:03.500
<i>when the shot went off.</i>

585
00:39:04.250 --> 00:39:05.208
[gunshot]

586
00:39:05.958 --> 00:39:08.208
[man 1] Grab that son of a bitch! Get him!

587
00:39:09.166 --> 00:39:11.125
[man 2] Don't let that bastard get away!

588
00:39:11.208 --> 00:39:13.833
[man 3] Kill that Conservative
son of bitch!

589
00:39:13.916 --> 00:39:15.916
[crowd clamoring]

590
00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:18.000
[somber music playing]

591
00:39:19.583 --> 00:39:22.416
[narrator] <i>Aureliano José</i>
<i>had been destined to find with her</i>

592
00:39:22.500 --> 00:39:25.291
<i>the happiness that Amaranta</i>
<i>had denied him.</i>

593
00:39:25.375 --> 00:39:30.041
<i>To have seven children</i>
<i>and to die in her arms of old age.</i>

594
00:39:33.208 --> 00:39:36.500
[gunshots]

595
00:39:59.291 --> 00:40:02.000
[narrator] <i>The other man's body</i>
<i>was so far gone</i>

596
00:40:02.083 --> 00:40:06.416
<i>that a patrol had to use a wheelbarrow</i>
<i>to carry away his remains.</i>

597
00:40:06.500 --> 00:40:09.875
<i>which had fallen apart</i>
<i>like bread soaked in water.</i>

598
00:40:14.333 --> 00:40:17.166
[in Latin] May his soul rest in peace.

599
00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:21.416
In the name of the Father.
and of the Son. and of the Holy Spirit.

600
00:40:22.250 --> 00:40:24.750
[in English] Rest in peace. my son.

601
00:40:24.833 --> 00:40:26.833
[Úrsula sobs]

602
00:41:05.958 --> 00:41:09.916
HUMAN VANITIES END HERE

603
00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:12.791
- [somber music continues]
- [rain pattering]

604
00:41:15.208 --> 00:41:16.583
[narrator] <i>Months later.</i>

605
00:41:16.666 --> 00:41:19.916
<i>Colonel Aureliano Buendía</i>
<i>returned to Macondo</i>

606
00:41:20.666 --> 00:41:24.250
<i>after committing</i>
<i>inconceivable acts of cruelty</i>

607
00:41:24.333 --> 00:41:27.250
<i>to quell his own officers' rebellion.</i>

608
00:41:30.416 --> 00:41:32.416
[thunder rumbling]

609
00:41:42.541 --> 00:41:45.750
[narrator] <i>He arrived in silence</i>
<i>and without an escort.</i>

610
00:41:46.750 --> 00:41:49.416
<i>wrapped in a blanket. despite the heat.</i>

611
00:41:50.208 --> 00:41:54.958
<i>exhausted by the uncertainty</i>
<i>and the vicious circle of the endless war.</i>

612
00:41:55.041 --> 00:41:57.791
<i>which always brought him back</i>
<i>to the same place.</i>

613
00:41:58.791 --> 00:42:02.416
<i>Only older. wearier.</i>

614
00:42:03.500 --> 00:42:08.375
<i>and no closer to knowing why.</i>
<i>how. or even when.</i>

615
00:42:13.083 --> 00:42:14.458
[music fades]

616
00:42:19.833 --> 00:42:22.166
It doesn't bother you
to share a table with a killer?

617
00:42:22.250 --> 00:42:23.416
Thank you.

618
00:42:27.625 --> 00:42:29.375
His own son was murdered because of him.

619
00:42:29.458 --> 00:42:31.708
Don't say that. Aureliano José was--

620
00:42:31.791 --> 00:42:34.083
He was murdered in vengeance
for the colonel's atrocities.

621
00:42:34.166 --> 00:42:35.416
They murdered him…

622
00:42:37.291 --> 00:42:40.416
because war is always more unfair
to the innocent.

623
00:42:42.458 --> 00:42:44.208
But all wars are like that.

624
00:43:02.250 --> 00:43:04.875
That's a list of
all of your other sons' names.

625
00:43:07.541 --> 00:43:10.250
Seventeen have come knocking so far.

626
00:43:10.333 --> 00:43:12.833
[intriguing music playing]

627
00:43:12.916 --> 00:43:14.458
[narrator] <i>The colonel then realized</i>

628
00:43:14.541 --> 00:43:18.333
<i>that the young boys and teenagers</i>
<i>he saw everywhere.</i>

629
00:43:19.416 --> 00:43:22.250
<i>that looked at him with his own eyes.</i>

630
00:43:23.333 --> 00:43:27.250
<i>were the children he had fathered</i>
<i>with women whose names he did not know.</i>

631
00:43:27.333 --> 00:43:28.541
[Gerineldo] Aureliano.

632
00:43:33.708 --> 00:43:35.416
How are you. son?

633
00:43:44.291 --> 00:43:47.625
[Gerineldo] We got word from the capital
that you had come back to Macondo.

634
00:43:48.916 --> 00:43:50.541
They sent another emissary.

635
00:43:52.166 --> 00:43:53.958
There are lawyers here to see you.

636
00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:01.041
[man 1] Mr. Buendía.

637
00:44:01.541 --> 00:44:03.458
We've come on behalf of the president.

638
00:44:03.541 --> 00:44:05.833
I know why you're here.
Let's get to the point.

639
00:44:06.791 --> 00:44:07.750
[man 1] Right.

640
00:44:09.416 --> 00:44:11.750
The president reiterates his commitment

641
00:44:11.833 --> 00:44:16.750
to grant you political participation
in all the towns you have liberated

642
00:44:16.833 --> 00:44:18.541
in exchange for these three things.

643
00:44:18.625 --> 00:44:20.666
- [Aureliano] I'm listening.
- All right.

644
00:44:22.208 --> 00:44:23.416
First and foremost.

645
00:44:23.500 --> 00:44:27.750
you must immediately renounce
any review of existing property titles.

646
00:44:28.875 --> 00:44:33.416
Secondly. you must renounce the fight
against clerical influence.

647
00:44:34.958 --> 00:44:37.958
And finally. you must renounce

648
00:44:38.041 --> 00:44:43.208
the aspirations of equal rights
between natural and illegitimate children

649
00:44:43.291 --> 00:44:46.291
to preserve and protect
household integrity.

650
00:44:52.708 --> 00:44:54.416
So what you're saying is

651
00:44:55.250 --> 00:44:57.083
that for the last 20 years.

652
00:44:58.083 --> 00:45:00.875
we've been fighting
for nothing more than power.

653
00:45:03.208 --> 00:45:04.250
[scoffs]

654
00:45:13.333 --> 00:45:14.833
Then show me where to sign.

655
00:45:16.583 --> 00:45:17.500
Pen. please.

656
00:45:18.083 --> 00:45:20.500
Here. Mr. Buendía. Here. Sign here.

657
00:45:20.583 --> 00:45:23.458
Excuse me. Colonel. but this is treason.

658
00:45:24.916 --> 00:45:26.916
[tense music playing]

659
00:45:28.291 --> 00:45:29.791
What did you just say. Gerineldo?

660
00:45:29.875 --> 00:45:32.083
That by signing this armistice

661
00:45:33.208 --> 00:45:35.708
you renounce everything we've fought for.

662
00:45:36.208 --> 00:45:38.166
And that makes you a traitor.

663
00:45:45.250 --> 00:45:47.125
Go say goodbye to your mother.

664
00:45:51.583 --> 00:45:52.750
From this point forward.

665
00:45:52.833 --> 00:45:54.958
you will have to answer
to the Council of War.

666
00:46:04.958 --> 00:46:06.916
Take care of your heart. Aureliano.

667
00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:08.916
because it's been rotting for years.
my friend.

668
00:46:22.958 --> 00:46:24.958
[door swings]

669
00:46:30.208 --> 00:46:31.625
[music fades]

670
00:46:45.083 --> 00:46:47.166
I know you plan to execute Gerineldo.

671
00:46:48.500 --> 00:46:50.833
And there's nothing I can do to stop you.

672
00:46:52.125 --> 00:46:54.458
But mark my words. Aureliano.

673
00:46:54.958 --> 00:46:57.333
the moment I see his body.

674
00:46:57.833 --> 00:47:01.791
I swear to you that.
on my father and my mother's bones…

675
00:47:03.833 --> 00:47:06.750
and on the memory of José Arcadio Buendía…

676
00:47:09.291 --> 00:47:11.750
I swear before God. Aureliano.

677
00:47:13.333 --> 00:47:16.000
that I will find you.
no matter where you go.

678
00:47:17.125 --> 00:47:20.250
and I will kill you with my own hands.

679
00:47:21.333 --> 00:47:23.458
The same way I would have done…

680
00:47:25.666 --> 00:47:28.208
if you'd come into the world
with a pig's tail.

681
00:47:28.291 --> 00:47:29.958
[sobs]

682
00:47:43.166 --> 00:47:45.000
[door opens]

683
00:48:03.916 --> 00:48:05.666
The farce is over. my friend.

684
00:48:06.541 --> 00:48:07.791
You're a free man.

685
00:48:08.666 --> 00:48:12.291
I'd rather die by firing squad
than see you become a traitor.

686
00:48:12.375 --> 00:48:13.416
Don't worry.

687
00:48:15.291 --> 00:48:17.000
You won't see me become a traitor.

688
00:48:21.916 --> 00:48:24.875
Get out of there
before the mosquitoes eat you alive.

689
00:48:27.208 --> 00:48:29.208
[intriguing music playing]

690
00:48:31.125 --> 00:48:36.000
ARMISTICE SIGNED BETWEEN THE GOVERNMENT
AND THE REBEL FORCES

691
00:48:46.708 --> 00:48:48.333
You are better than ever. Colonel.

692
00:48:48.833 --> 00:48:50.875
You could fight 30 more wars.

693
00:48:51.625 --> 00:48:54.291
[Aureliano] Can you show me
exactly where my heart is. Doctor?

694
00:48:55.791 --> 00:48:57.666
Everyone tells me it's rotten.

695
00:49:04.583 --> 00:49:05.625
Allow me.

696
00:49:16.291 --> 00:49:18.291
[music intensifies]

697
00:49:45.083 --> 00:49:46.291
What's all this?

698
00:49:48.916 --> 00:49:50.625
Great-Grandfather's projects.

699
00:49:55.333 --> 00:49:56.458
Did he make these?

700
00:49:57.166 --> 00:50:00.208
Some he did.
but he almost drove Great-Grandma crazy.

701
00:50:00.708 --> 00:50:02.833
Just like how you will
if you keep distracting me.

702
00:50:04.375 --> 00:50:06.458
[narrator] <i>José Arcadio Segundo never knew</i>

703
00:50:06.541 --> 00:50:10.458
<i>that what he found</i>
<i>would change the fate of Macondo.</i>

704
00:50:11.125 --> 00:50:12.250
[knocking at door]

705
00:50:12.916 --> 00:50:14.666
[José Arcadio II] Get the door. Aureliano.

706
00:50:14.750 --> 00:50:15.833
[Aureliano II] Hang on.

707
00:50:20.250 --> 00:50:21.291
[music stops]

708
00:50:21.375 --> 00:50:24.583
Why the long face. José Arcadio?
Let's go celebrate peace.

709
00:50:24.666 --> 00:50:27.875
[narrator] <i>Although people</i>
<i>frequently confused him with his brother.</i>

710
00:50:28.375 --> 00:50:31.666
<i>that day. Aureliano Segundo</i>
<i>didn't correct her.</i>

711
00:50:31.750 --> 00:50:33.750
[mysterious organ music playing]

712
00:51:05.666 --> 00:51:06.875
Good morning. Colonel.

713
00:51:07.375 --> 00:51:08.916
We're glad you could make it.

714
00:51:10.250 --> 00:51:11.708
Listen. before I sign.

715
00:51:12.708 --> 00:51:14.375
I have one final request.

716
00:51:17.250 --> 00:51:19.458
I want to ensure that my men

717
00:51:19.541 --> 00:51:22.125
receive a pension
as the war veterans they are.

718
00:51:22.625 --> 00:51:25.333
and for you to recognize us
as a legitimate army.

719
00:51:26.875 --> 00:51:31.000
That's all I ask for
in exchange for total surrender.

720
00:51:34.458 --> 00:51:36.000
Not to worry. Colonel.

721
00:51:36.958 --> 00:51:38.208
You have my word.

722
00:51:42.125 --> 00:51:43.125
This way.

723
00:52:28.958 --> 00:52:30.958
[music intensifies]

724
00:52:52.083 --> 00:52:53.333
Aureliano.

725
00:52:54.333 --> 00:52:56.333
[tense music playing]

726
00:53:18.041 --> 00:53:20.041
[gunshot echoes]

727
00:53:22.125 --> 00:53:24.125
[music intensifies]

728
00:53:39.916 --> 00:53:41.916
[music fades]

729
00:53:42.750 --> 00:53:44.750
[dramatic music playing]

730
00:54:39.791 --> 00:54:41.791
[music fades]

731
00:54:44.041 --> 00:54:46.041
[mysterious rhythmic music playing]

732
00:56:36.291 --> 00:56:37.416
[music fades]

733
00:56:37.500 --> 00:56:39.500
[dark ethereal music playing]

